-- title:
--   Meet order with an idele trivial at v has the same local box
-- statement:
--   Fix rationals $a,b$ and write $\mathbb{H}=\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ for the associated quaternion algebra. Let $R$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule of $\mathbb{H}$ which is an order in the sense of the project predicate [`QuaternionAlgebra.IsOrder`](def/QuaternionAlgebra_Order.html#L11), i.e. $1\in R$, $R$ is closed under multiplication, its $\mathbb{Q}$-span is all of $\mathbb{H}$, and it is finitely generated. Let $q$ be a prime, let $v$ be a height-one prime of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $q\in v$, and let $sf$ be a unit of $\mathbb{H}\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q},f}$ (the finite adele ring of $\mathbb{Q}$), subject to the hypothesis that for every height-one prime $u$ containing $q$ the component of $sf$ at $u$, i.e. the image of $sf$ under the base-changed evaluation map $\mathbb{H}\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q},f}\to\mathbb{H}\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_u$, equals $1$. The conclusion is an equality of additive subgroups of $\mathbb{H}\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_v$: the local box at $v$ of the meet order $R\sqcap \mathrm{conjByFiniteIdele}(R,sf)$ — the intersection of $R$ with the submodule of elements of $\mathbb{H}$ whose image in $\mathbb{H}\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q},f}$ lies in $sf\,\widehat{R}\,sf^{-1}$, where $\widehat{R}$ is the finite adelic box of $R$ — coincides with the local box at $v$ of $R$, the subgroup generated by the elements $z\otimes c$ with $z$ in the order and $c$ in the valuation ring of $\mathbb{Q}_v$.
--
--   This is the statement that passing from an order to a meet order $R\cap sf\widehat{R}sf^{-1}$ does not change the completion at a place $v$ at which the conjugating idele is trivial; no condition is imposed on the components of $sf$ away from the primes above $q$. It is used in the construction of the Čerednik–Drinfeld tower at $q$, where all levels of the tower are required to have the same local data at $v$, and is cited by [`CerednikDrinfeld.CosetGraph.exists_quot_equiv_classSet_shift_forget_of_mumfordSideFrame`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.CosetGraph.exists_quot_equiv_classSet_shift_forget_of_mumfordSideFrame).
